# Snake App Cursor Rule

Flutter game app: offline-first Snake with responsive play, local profile saves, and platform-correct controls.
Follow these standards for consistent contributions across developers and AI agents.

## Scope and stack
- App root: repository root (`lib/`, `test/`, `android/`, `ios/`, `linux/`, `macos/`, `windows/`, `web/`)
- Package ID: `chingalo.family.snake_app` · Display name: **Snake App**
- Stack: Flutter, local SQLite via **Drift (`AppDatabase`)**, SharedPreferences via **PreferenceService**, audio (SFX/BGM), Provider or Riverpod
- Target layout: `lib/app/`, `lib/core/`, `lib/modules/<feature>/{page,components,utils}`, `lib/shared/` (see `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`)
- Product: `docs/PRODUCT_REQUIREMENTS.md` · Technical: `docs/TECHNICAL_REQUIREMENTS.md` · Flow: `docs/APP_FLOW.md` · UX: `docs/UI_UX_DESIGN_BRIEF.md` · Schema: `docs/BACKEND_SCHEMA.md` · Plan: `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` · Architecture: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`
- Skills: `.cursor/skills/snake-app-project/`, `snake-app-gameplay/`, `snake-app-offline-profile/`, `snake-app-community-docs/`

## Required workflow before finishing a task
1. **Check what changed** - `git status` and `git diff`; only intentional files
2. Run `flutter analyze` - must report **no errors**. Do not mark the task done until this passes.
3. **Tests after any `lib/` change** - run `flutter test` before finishing:
   - Prefer full `flutter test` when touching audio, core services, game engine, persistence/profile, providers/bootstrap, or when unsure
   - Narrow `flutter test test/<area>_test.dart` is OK only for clearly isolated UI/string tweaks with an existing focused test
   - Do not mark the task done until analyze **and** tests pass
4. If product scope, UX, architecture, schema, CI, or plan conventions changed, update the matching `docs/` files in the same change set:
   - `docs/PRODUCT_REQUIREMENTS.md` - scope and success criteria
   - `docs/TECHNICAL_REQUIREMENTS.md` - stack, quality gates, CI, preference keys
   - `docs/APP_FLOW.md` - routes and screen flow
   - `docs/UI_UX_DESIGN_BRIEF.md` - palette, screen rules, feedback
   - `docs/BACKEND_SCHEMA.md` - Drift tables and local stores
   - `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` - shipped modules and acceptance
   - `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` - structure, packages, layers
   - `README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md` - install commands, features, stack, contributor workflow
   - `SECURITY.md`, `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`, `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/`, `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` - contacts, platforms, CI checklists
5. If stack, CI commands, project layout, prefs keys, or store listings changed, follow `.cursor/skills/snake-app-community-docs/SKILL.md` in the same change set
6. If marketing-facing product facts change (level count, game modes, controls, offline/profile claims, store links), also update sibling website docs at `../snake-app-website/docs/` when that repo is present beside this checkout
7. If this rule or skills drift from the codebase, update `.cursor/` in the same change set
8. Desktop CI lives in `.github/workflows/` - see `docs/TECHNICAL_REQUIREMENTS.md` when changing build/release behavior

## Product constraints (do not regress)
- Offline-first: high scores and levels persist locally; no DHIS2 auth for core play
- Profile required to **save** scores/levels; play without profile is allowed
- Touch: swipe · Desktop (Linux/macOS/Windows): arrow keys
- Playground must work on phone/tablet including rotation
- SFX and background music are **separate** settings toggles
- UI languages: English (default) and Kiswahili via Flutter gen-l10n (`lib/l10n/`)
- Android updates: prefer Play Store / in-app update - not custom APK sideload for MVP
- Theme: nature-arcade greens/amber from `docs/UI_UX_DESIGN_BRIEF.md` - avoid purple-indigo defaults

## Architecture conventions
- Domain logic in `lib/core/services/` or feature controllers - not in widgets
- Grid metrics from layout constraints - not fixed portrait-only sizes
- Package imports: `package:snake_app/...`
- Prefer shared widgets in `lib/shared/` or `lib/core/` before one-offs
- User-facing strings: ARB + `context.l10n` - no hardcoded UI English
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, keystores, API keys)

## Naming
- Modules: `lib/modules/<module>/` with optional `components/` and `utils/`
- Tests: mirror under `test/`
- **Variables must be meaningful** (domain words, not abbreviations)
  - Indexes: `rowIndex`, `cellIndex`, `levelIndex` - never bare `i`/`j`/`k`
  - Avoid: `snap`, `db`, `tp`, `rng`, `item`, `info`, `data`, `tmp` when a clearer name exists
  - Booleans: `is…` / `has…` / `can…`
  - Prefer `engineSnapshot`, `levelConfig`, `eatEvent`, `sharedPreferences`, `packageInfo`
  - OK idioms: `context`, `ref`, `child`, `theme`, `_`

## Pull request quality bar
- Scoped, reviewable diffs
- Tests for game logic, unlock rules, and persistence gates
- Show analyze/tests ran and `git status` reviewed
